usage: mach [global arguments] xpcshell-test [command arguments]

Run XPCOM Shell tests (API direct unit testing)

Global Arguments:
  -v, --verbose         Print verbose output.
  -q, --quiet           Don't print as much output.
  -l, --log-file FILENAME
                        Filename to write log data to.
  --log-interval        Prefix log line with interval from last message rather
                        than relative time. Note that this is NOT execution
                        time if there are parallel operations.
  --no-interactive      Automatically selects the default option on any
                        interactive prompts. If the output is not a terminal,
                        then --no-interactive is assumed.
  --log-no-times        Do not prefix log lines with times. By default, mach
                        will prefix each output line with the time since
                        command start.
  -h, --help            Show this help message.
  --debug-command       Start a Python debugger when command is dispatched.
  --profile-command     Capture a Python profile of the mach process as
                        command is dispatched.
  --settings FILENAME   Path to settings file.

Command Parameters:
  testPaths             Paths of tests to run.

Command Arguments:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --app-binary APP_BINARY
                        path to application binary (eg: c:\program
                        files\mozilla firefox\firefox.exe)
  --app-path APPPATH    application directory (as opposed to XRE directory)
  --msix-app-path MSIXAPPPATH
                        application directory for msix mode (as opposed to XRE
                        directory)
  --msix-app-binary MSIX_APP_BINARY
                        path to application binary for msix mode (eg:
                        c:\program files\mozilla firefox\firefox.exe)
  --interactive         don't automatically run tests, drop to an xpcshell
                        prompt
  --verbose             always print stdout and stderr from tests
  --verbose-if-fails    Output the log if a test fails, even when run in
                        parallel
  --keep-going          continue running tests after test killed with
                        control-C (SIGINT)
  --logfiles            create log files (default, only used to override --no-
                        logfiles)
  --dump-tests DUMP_TESTS
                        Specify path to a filename to dump all the tests that
                        will be run
  --manifest MANIFEST   Manifest of test directories to use
  --no-logfiles         don't create log files
  --sequential          Run all tests sequentially
  --temp-dir TEMPDIR    Directory to use for temporary files
  --testing-modules-dir TESTINGMODULESDIR
                        Directory where testing modules are located.
  --profile-name PROFILENAME
                        name of application profile being tested
  --build-info-json MOZINFO
                        path to a mozinfo.json including information about the
                        build configuration. defaults to looking for
                        mozinfo.json next to the script.
  --shuffle             Execute tests in random order
  --xre-path XREPATH    absolute path to directory containing XRE (probably
                        xulrunner)
  --msix-xre-path MSIXXREPATH
                        absolute path to directory containing XRE in msix mode
                        (probably xulrunner)
  --symbols-path SYMBOLSPATH
                        absolute path to directory containing breakpad
                        symbols, or the URL of a zip file containing symbols
  --jscov-dir-prefix JSCOVDIR
                        Directory to store per-test javascript line coverage
                        data as json.
  --debugger DEBUGGER   use the given debugger to launch the application
  --debugger-args DEBUGGERARGS
                        pass the given args to the debugger _before_ the
                        application on the command line
  --debugger-interactive
                        prevents the test harness from redirecting stdout and
                        stderr for interactive debuggers
  --jsdebugger          Waits for a devtools JS debugger to connect before
                        starting the test.
  --jsdebugger-port JSDEBUGGERPORT
                        The port to listen on for a debugger connection if
                        --jsdebugger is specified.
  --tag TEST_TAGS       filter out tests that don't have the given tag. Can be
                        used multiple times in which case the test must
                        contain at least one of the given tags.
  --utility-path UTILITY_PATH
                        Path to a directory containing utility programs, such
                        as stack fixer scripts.
  --xpcshell XPCSHELL   Path to xpcshell binary
  --http3server HTTP3SERVER
                        Path to http3server binary
  --rerun-failures      Rerun failures from the previous run, if any
  --failure-manifest FAILURE_MANIFEST
                        Path to a manifest file from which to rerun failures
                        (with --rerun-failure) or in which to record failed
                        tests
  --threads THREADCOUNT
                        override the number of jobs (threads) when running
                        tests in parallel, the default is CPU x 1.5 when
                        running via mach and CPU x 4 when running in
                        automation
  --timeout-factor TIMEOUTFACTOR
                        multiplier for test timeout values
  --variant VARIANT     use specified variant for any harness level changes.
  --setpref PREF=VALUE  Defines an extra user preference (can be passed
                        multiple times.
  --setenv NAME=VALUE   Set one or more environment variable before launching
                        the test (can be passed multiple times).
  --verify              Run tests in verification mode: Run many times in
                        different ways, to see if there are intermittent
                        failures.
  --verify-max-time VERIFYMAXTIME
                        Maximum time, in seconds, to run in --verify mode.
  --headless            Enable headless mode by default for tests which don't
                        specify whether to use headless mode
  --conditioned-profile
                        Run with conditioned profile instead of fresh blank
                        profile
  --self-test           Run self tests
  --run-failures RUNFAILURES
                        Run failures matching keyword
  --timeout-as-pass     Harness level timeouts will be treated as passing
  --crash-as-pass       Harness level crashes will be treated as passing
  --disable-fission     disable fission mode (back to e10s || 1proc)
  --repeat REPEAT       repeat the test X times, default [0]
  --profiler            Run the Firefox Profiler and get a performance profile
                        of the test. This is useful to find performance
                        issues, and also to see what exactly the test is
                        doing.
  --force               Force reinstallation of test symlinks even if up to
                        date.

Output Logging:
  Each option represents a possible logging format and takes a filename to
  write that format to, or '-' to write to stdout. Some options are provided
  by the mozlog utility; see https://firefox-source-
  docs.mozilla.org/mozbase/mozlog.html for extended documentation.

  --log-raw LOG_RAW     Raw structured log messages (provided by mozlog)
  --log-unittest LOG_UNITTEST
                        Unittest style output (provided by mozlog)
  --log-xunit LOG_XUNIT
                        xUnit compatible XML (provided by mozlog)
  --log-html LOG_HTML   HTML report (provided by mozlog)
  --log-mach LOG_MACH   Human-readable output (provided by mozlog)
  --log-tbpl LOG_TBPL   TBPL style log format (provided by mozlog)
  --log-grouped LOG_GROUPED
                        Grouped summary of test results (provided by mozlog)
  --log-raw-level LOG_RAW_LEVEL
                        A least log level to subscribe to for the given
                        formatter (debug, info, error, etc.)
  --log-raw-unexpectedonly
                        Suppress process output for tests with expected
                        results.
  --log-mach-verbose    Enables verbose mode for the given formatter.
  --log-mach-level LOG_MACH_LEVEL
                        A least log level to subscribe to for the given
                        formatter (debug, info, error, etc.)
  --log-mach-buffer LOG_MACH_BUFFER
                        If specified, enables message buffering at the given
                        buffer size limit.
  --log-mach-screenshot
                        Enable logging reftest-analyzer compatible screenshot
                        data.
  --log-mach-no-screenshot
                        Disable logging reftest-analyzer compatible screenshot
                        data.
  --log-mach-unexpectedonly
                        Suppress process output for tests with expected
                        results.
  --log-tbpl-compact    Enables compact mode for the given formatter.
  --log-tbpl-level LOG_TBPL_LEVEL
                        A least log level to subscribe to for the given
                        formatter (debug, info, error, etc.)
  --log-tbpl-buffer LOG_TBPL_BUFFER
                        If specified, enables message buffering at the given
                        buffer size limit.
  --log-tbpl-unexpectedonly
                        Suppress process output for tests with expected
                        results.
